{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":313200,"duration_api_ms":453891,"num_turns":24,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e1ac77b2-60f2-40a7-b884-e42e15029913","total_cost_usd":1.73211035,"usage":{"input_tokens":3783,"cache_creation_input_tokens":57630,"cache_read_input_tokens":733387,"output_tokens":8075,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":57630,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3783,"outputTokens":8075,"cacheReadInputTokens":733387,"cacheCreationInputTokens":57630,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9476710000000003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5923,"outputTokens":23937,"cacheReadInputTokens":3279351,"cacheCreationInputTokens":264717,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7844393500000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"In `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs` lines 978-987, the `ShrimpHatched` event message includes only the count of hatched clutches/juveniles but does not log which suppression factors limited `hatch_rate`. In contrast, the `EggFailure` event (lines 996-1032) does diagnose causes (LowOxygen, HighTemperature, LowMinerals, etc.). When hatch_rate is mediocre (e.g. 0.4) but some clutches succeed, users see hatched events without any indication of which factor is dragging hatch success down. Add the same cause-tagging logic used for EggFailure to ShrimpHatched events when hatch_rate < some threshold (e.g. 0.8), so partial-success hatches also explain their limiting factors.","rationale":"The acceptance criteria require that 'debug output, events, or snapshots identify which factors suppressed reproduction in failing scenarios so tuning remains explainable.' Successful-but-suppressed hatches (hatch_rate well below 1.0) currently have no factor attribution in events, only in the snapshot's single dominant_repro_suppression label. A tank with 40% hatch success is effectively failing at reproduction but the hatch events give no diagnosis."},{"body":"In `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs` line 1530, the `condition` factor in `reproductive_readiness_factors` uses `state.animal.adult.condition_index` directly (range 0.0-1.0 from update_condition clamping at line 453). However, there is no minimum floor applied, unlike density (floor 0.05), TAN (floor 0.05), and nitrite (floor 0.05). At condition_index = 0.0, the product of all 8 factors becomes exactly 0.0, making reproductive_readiness_target 0.0. Combined with the EMA smoothing, this creates a very long recovery time since `readiness += 0.1 * (target - readiness)` starting from 0.0 requires many days to climb back. Consider applying a floor (e.g. 0.05) to the condition factor for consistency with other factors, or document the intentional lack of floor.","rationale":"All other stressor factors (density, TAN, NO2, minerals) have explicit minimum floors (0.05 or 0.3) to prevent the multiplicative product from being driven to exactly zero by a single factor. Condition reaching 0.0 zeros out the entire readiness product indefinitely. While biologically plausible that starving shrimp don't breed, the zero-floor creates an asymmetry with other factors and an unusually sticky zero state due to EMA smoothing."},{"body":"The `test_chemistry_stress_suppresses_breeding` test (reproduction_factors.rs line 445) covers TAN and NO2 independently as required by the acceptance criteria, but does not independently verify low-GH suppression of breeding. The acceptance criteria state 'Water chemistry: very low GH, high TAN, or high NO2 suppress breeding' and the reviewer unit test list does not have a separate GH test. GH is tested only indirectly via `test_all_reproduction_factors_are_named_parameters` (which verifies parameter sensitivity) and via the mineral suppression snapshot label tests. Add an explicit assertion within `test_chemistry_stress_suppresses_breeding` (or a sibling test) that shows very low GH (e.g. 1-2 dGH) independently suppresses breeding readiness below the clean baseline.","rationale":"The acceptance criteria explicitly name 'very low GH' as a breeding suppression factor alongside TAN and NO2. While the code implements GH suppression correctly via `gh_mineral_factor`, the dedicated chemistry stress test only exercises TAN and NO2. An explicit GH test strengthens the coverage and guards against regressions in the GH→readiness pathway."}],"summary":"The reproduction factors implementation is well-engineered and comprehensive. All 8 suppression factors (temperature, condition, minerals, stability, molt stress, density, TAN, nitrite) are correctly implemented with proper division-by-zero guards (.max(0.01)), bounds clamping, and multiplicative compounding. All factors are fully configurable via TOML parameters with no hardcoded magic numbers. The stability tracker uses asymmetric EMA smoothing and separate egg-drop pathways. Save/load handles migration from older schemas. All 17 reproduction tests pass. The EggFailure event IS emitted (lines 996-1032) with diagnostic causes. Three minor issues identified: (1) ShrimpHatched events lack factor diagnostics unlike EggFailure events, creating an observability gap for partial-success breeding; (2) the condition factor lacks a minimum floor unlike other factors, allowing it to zero out the entire readiness product; (3) the chemistry stress test doesn't independently verify low-GH suppression despite it being named in the acceptance criteria."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"af15fbf8-2e2f-4cb5-88d6-65003aaee444"}
